  "number": 100,
  "meaning": "The number 100 symbolizes completeness, the fulfillment of God's promises, and an abundance of blessing in biblical tradition.",
  "description": "Abraham received his son Isaac when he was 100 years old, highlighting God's faithfulness and ability to fulfill His promises even when it seems humanly impossible (Gen 21:5). In Jesus' parable of the sower, good soil yields a hundredfold harvest, symbolizing maximum fruitfulness and blessing (Matt 13:8; Mark 4:8). The number one hundred thus represents complete abundance—both in God's fulfillment of His promises and in the spiritual fruit that grows in those who receive His word.",
